e Orphanet concept, so it was modeled with `MONDO:equivalentObsolete`.\n+- The previous GARD reference was non-functional and was the only support for the original label, so it was removed.\n+\n+Checks completed:\n+\n+- Read the imported issue context and followed the issue-thread resolution rather than the original title/body alone.\n+- Verified existing MONDO usage patterns for `MONDO:includedEntryInOMIM` and `MONDO:equivalentObsolete` before adding new xrefs.\n+- Confirmed `OMIM:612541` is already used elsewhere in MONDO in the related G6PC3-associated term context.\n+- Ran `robot convert --catalog src/ontology/catalog-v001.xml -i src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o /tmp/opencode/mondo-edit.TMP.obo` successfully as a syntax check.\n+\n+Validation note:\n+\n+- I could not run the repo’s requested `make NORM` Docker-based normalization step because `docker` is not available in this environment. The ontology edit was still syntax-checked successfully with local `robot convert`.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Updated `MONDO:0023124` to keep the term rather than obsolete it, relabeling it to `Dursun syndrome` in line with the issue discussion. Also removed the obsolete-candidate/GARD-based metadata and added the discussed xrefs for `OMIM:612541` as `MONDO:includedEntryInOMIM` and `Orphanet:178503` as `MONDO:equivalentObsolete`.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-a